Z||000079||MinnGreenGT||12-17-2001||05:42 PM||||[Edited in light of Tgowens following post=RCB]<P>There is currently discussion occuring about whether or not it is the right time to schedule a regional show for CFOG-i... not because of FOCOA or the people putting on the Reno/Lk.Tahoe show, but out of consideration for Fiero owners- and not forcing them to commit to one or the other (not everyone can afford the travel time/distance/expense of multiple "big shows" in a short period of time). But again, this is currently under consideration and discussion.<P>And do forgive me if any of the above info is not 100% correct... This is just how I'm understanding the current situation.<P>As to the info about the PowerFest... that is an event which Turbo88 has volunteered to head up (along with Archie's assistance/competition  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">). If he wishes the assistance/backing of CFOG-i, he is certainly welcomed discuss it with us! But, if you read the thread you listed, you'd know that this is the case- and that Turbo88 himself has yet to repond to the thread as of recent (sept.20th was his last response)<p>[This message has been edited by MinnGreenGT (edited 12-17-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000080||tgowens||12-17-2001||05:47 PM||||Well, as I understand the latest rumours, FOCOA <I>is</I> backing the GGF/RCNV show in Tahoe. Nevertheless, it may just be that CFOG-International will make other arrangements at such time as it would be more convenient for Fiero Owners.<P>Also, worth looking into is the Fiero Power Tour that Eric mentioned. CFOG-International intends to provide and participate in all aspects of the appeal of the Fiero for its members.<P>By the way, Eric, I can't seem to locate the membership applications for you and Chris or the application for your club .. did you send them?||||reg||1
Z||000081||West Coast Fiero||12-17-2001||07:25 PM||||barely any members of our club even know the politics and development of a new International club, other than Anthony, Chris, and I ( hell, Chris and I havent even turned in our dues for <B>OUR OWN</B> club, let alone a parent club. were just a bunch of slackers. I myself have found no reason not to join, but never the less I <B>WILL</B> bombard you guys with tech articles to fill your newsletters as I have countless HTML files of fix-it info, besides it will give me a chance to start my portfolio for my journalism class.<P> I <I>think</I> Chris' general position is that he wants to wait to see where the club goes before he and others of Fieros West pitch in any funds, and <I>honestly,</I>it's hard to see anything now after Georges child-like anticks ( we all make mistakes, but why make every body else suffer for it ).<P> But I honestly think CFOG-I should start off with either sponsering this Power Tour, or make something so significant out here on the West Coast, that it would put the Dell's and every East Coast event to shame - cause lets face it, West Coast support, follow through, and events flat out <FONT COLOR="red"><B>SUCK</B></FONT>compared to the east coast, and even mid west.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://clubs.hemmings.com/fieroswest/WestCoast300.gif">  <BR>Eric Nelson<BR>Technician,<BR>West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111<p>[This message has been edited by West Coast Fiero (edited 12-17-2001).]||||reg||1
