Z||000086||Archie||12-18-2001||02:46 AM||||Whew.... I just sat here and read this whole thread.<P>Not that anyone cares, but I thought I'd offer my opinion on all that has been said.<P>First off, I'd like to explain why I even bothered to look at this thread. The title of this thread "Let's talk about FOCOA" is what attracted me. At first I thought "What a terrible title for a thread about an alternate Club that claims to be interested in pulling the whole Fiero Community together". I really don't think it's a great idea to "talk about" someone else when he's not here. But, as I read thru the thread, I'm remembering the the things fPhil has been telling people, privately and publicly, about me and my business. Over the years he has told people that I'm an alcoholic, that I've filed bankruptcy several times, he's said that I owe him a bunch of money, he has even stated in his newsletter that I was out of business (even though he knew better via letters to him from my customers) & these are the nice things he's said about me.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> I paid for a lifetime membership back in 1989 but haven't seen a newsletter since like 1993 or something. So, in reality, I don't really care if you guys want to bash him until the cows come home. Anyone who has met fPhil and thinks that he is a "good guy", doesn't really know him very well. <P>As I read thru the thread, I see that several of the CFOG-I regional directors are people that I have a lot of respect for, & this is a good sign. <P>FIERO JOHN-WI, said it best & I agree with him on the first 4 of 5 points he makes. I truely believe that on point 5 the answer should be MIDWEST FIERO REGIONAL.<P>IMHO, CFOG-I has a very strong base of Regional Directors, the weakness is at the top. DON'T flame me yet....... hear me out. tgowens, wether you like it or not your name and past actions/comments too closely aligns you with the Fiero Shop & the in-fighting of the various CA Fiero groups. Everybody knows that the various California Fiero factions have spent the last several years fighting among yourselves. A person would need a scorecard to keep track of who is backstabbing who out there. Wether you like it or not, there is no perception of continuity among all the different groups out there trying to "one-up" each other. The latest exchange between tgowans and Eric is the latest example that you guys in CA can't get yourselves all on one page let alone run a National non-political organization. The powers that be at CFOG-I would be well served to TOTALLY drop the politics and make an honest study of the people and Clubs in the Mid-West. Take a look at the WI, NIFE, Heartland, IA & MI clubs and you'll see that there are NO internal politics that interfere with putting on successful, well attended events. I've belonged to many automotive clubs over the years and they all had the politics thing keeping them from being successful. When I moved up here to Chicago, I joined NIFE and, in the last 5 years, I've attended almost all the shows in the Mid-West. I can tell you for sure that these groups don't have the politics getting in the way of success. I know that our Clubs out here just so called "Regional" Clubs, but I'll put the "Regional" Dell's Run show up against any show any place else in the country. If you haven't ever attended the Dells show, you have absolutely no idea how well run and organized and politics free a show can be.<P>What would I recommend to make CFOG-I a success?<P>Well, you're not gonna like it but this is it...<P>tgowens, I know that CFOG-I is "your" Club.... or at least that it's your idea. For the good of the club, this is what you need to do.<P>1) tgowens: you gotta resign..... you have a good group of regional directors, have them elect one of themselves to replace you. They can then setup elections for maybe a year from now and you can then run for election.<P>2) CFOG-I: You must try to drop the politics. If you were interested in backing a particular show and another group decided to back a show before you did, why don't you still consider backing that show. I mean if it was a good enough of a show to consider in the first place, why wouldn't you still want to support it? "Politics"<P>3) Learn how to put on a show... pay attention to the regional directors, between them they been to a lot of shows and have a lot of input to offer. If you haven't put on a successful local show, why would anyone pay National dues to see you flop with a national show. <P>4) Relations with businesses: there shouldn't be any nor should there be any perception that there is ANY business behind the Club. The only merchandizing the club should do is for club "T" shirts etc. This is how FOCOA started out, he sold a few belt buckels & T shirts and had other businesses (like myself) advertize in his newsletter. Then when he made copies of the Zumwalt kit, he stopped taking my ads and started telling people I was out of business.<P>5) Also, publish a couple of newsletters before you tell some business that he has to pay $100 for some little ad in a newsletter that hasn't even had it's first copy published yet.<P>I hope this is of some help...... I know that there will be a few people who want quote one line of what I've said and flame me for it. <P>And you are right, tgowens, I don't like you a hell of a lot & I don't care for George even a little bit.... but until you take the CA style politics out of this, it will be "your" club and not a national club.<P>One last thing.... if you don't mind.... we are all Fiero enthusiasts, yet you guys out there still find some reason not to get along with each other. I'm sure I speak for most people in the Mid-West clubs when I say that until you learn to work together, please don't move to our part of the country and try to screw our clubs up.<P>BTW, I would like to invite anyone who is really interested in getting nice newsletters "on time" & being associated with nice Fiero people to consider joining the the WI, IL, MI & IA Fiero clubs..... you'll find that they have a lot to offer to members that are not in the region.<P>Archie<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000087||2M4 Dale||12-18-2001||08:30 AM||||Hey Archie, I have a couple of points to make.<P>1st point I would like to make is ... This new club CFOG-I was not just Terrys idea.......Cheever3000 and several other fellows from this forum, myself included, were in the planning stages of a new international club when we found that Terry and his group were heading down the same path. Terry and his group were considerably farther along than us (website etc.) so, after a great amount of talking, we joined forces. So even though Terry is the Chairman and "one" of the founders for this club ... this is not "his" club ... It is "our" club.<P>2nd point to make is that anytime you involve more than 3 people in a group ... your gonna have politics....sucks but it's the way humans work.<P>3rd point, and this is unrelated.....I have a 355 four bolt on a stand in my garage....I'll be talking to you more in the near future ... lol||||reg||7
Z||000088||fierobear||12-18-2001||08:28 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by tgowens:<BR><B>Well, as I understand the latest rumours, FOCOA <I>is</I> backing the GGF/RCNV show in Tahoe. Nevertheless, it may just be that CFOG-International will make other arrangements at such time as it would be more convenient for Fiero Owners.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I am working on a location, banquet facility and accomodatins for a show in the Tahoe area. FOCOA is not involved. The presidents of the clubs in the west are organizing, Larry Hughes (president of San Diego) is the coordinator.<P>I wanted to have a date and place 2 months ago, but Tahoe is proving to be a difficult and expensive place to hold a show. I'm currently looking at North Tahoe and Truckee.||||reg||1
Z||000089||tgowens||12-18-2001||09:23 PM||||John, let me know if I can help in any way.......||||reg||1
Z||000090||mbramble||12-18-2001||10:16 PM||||Archie, I certainly have to agree with you.  I thought it was a lousey way to drum up support for a new club -- by bashing an old one.  Even if FOCOA was, or is, the absolute worst 'organization' on the planet, how good do you look by saying you are better than that?  Wow, a club that is better than the worst.  I have nothing at all to do with any club at this momement and don't know if I will.  However, I can say that I will certainly have nothing to do with this new group as long as tgowens is in the 'leadership'.  Don't know him, have never met him but have just seen too many posts of his concerning his involvement/non-involvement with The Fiero Shop.  And I don't care if he is or isn't involved with it, it was just the tone and positions taken in all those posts.||||reg||1
Z||000091||2M4 Dale||12-19-2001||12:13 AM||||Hey Guys ... hold on here a minute. All we wanted was to get a grasp of what you all (members of Pennocks) thought about the way FOCOA was doing things and try to get a bearing on how we want to do things differently. Not nessasarily bash FOCOA. Once again and I hope this can be understood by all......we do not intend to replace FOCOA we only wish to provide a viable alternative to them.<P>Plus, I know Terry personally. He is a great guy !!! He was associated with Fiero Shop to some degree at one time...but not now. Terry is very matter of fact. If you could talk with him face to face you would be able to hear the inflections in his voice and see the expressions on his face..(seems kinda soft spoken and calm most of the time)..can't do that on a printed word forum. I don't read the flame war posts so I don't quite know what he has said to tick everyone off BUT I'm sure that was never his intent ...at all.<P>OK now that I'm done defending my club and the clubs chairman........you can join us by visiting our website...  <A HREF="http://www.cfog-i.org/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.cfog-i.org/</A>   ... We are gonna make into a great Fiero club !!! You can watch and see or help us become great tonight !!! All we need is YOU. ||||reg||4
Z||000092||West Coast Fiero||12-19-2001||12:21 AM||||mbramble, though I fully understand your stand point - but are you willing to defend an organization that has done nothing for <B> YOU </B>. Granted, I personally know Phil on a first name basis, but he himself couldnt give a crap about <B>HIS OWN</B> organization, let alone any other one. Want to debate what I have to say - <B>FINE</B>, but I honestly think you will be the only one with any other views other than my own - actually, I woult like to hear any other views<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://clubs.hemmings.com/fieroswest/WestCoast300.gif">  <BR>Eric Nelson<BR>Technician,<BR>West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111<p>[This message has been edited by West Coast Fiero (edited 12-19-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000093||WKDFIRO||12-19-2001||01:16 AM||||I find it startling that I would agree with Archie on anything. But I whole heartedly agree with Archie on the topic of politics.<P>I knew that there would be trouble as soon as I saw the subject line of the e-mail "Let's Talk about FOCOA." It did seem to be a contradiction to stay out of a fire fight while bashing someone. Its another point I agree with. <P>But I do find it very interesting to see an outsiders view on "California Fiero factions" and how we are fighting each other. Currently the Presidents of San Diego (Fieros of San Diego), LA (Fieros West), Nevada, (Fiero Road Club) and San Francisco (Golden Gate Fieros) are working together to organize a show as John mentioned. Silver State Fieros as well as Arizona Fieros are supporting us and will most likely be there to help at the show. I don't right recall at least Fieros West having ANY problems with any of the fore mentioned clubs at all. In San Leandro it was actually Joe who stuck all the Presidents at the head table for the first time. It became very apparent that the "rowdy" table fast became the one with the Presidents on it. CFOG president Brian Morgan was with us too and had a great time. <P>Eric who happens to be a part of Fieros West's Activities Coordinators does not embody the whole of California Fiero Factions. Terry who happens to be a part of CFOGI does not embody the whole of California Fiero Factions.<P>Sure, they are some of the louder sections of California Fiero Factions, I count myself as one of those vocal people. If anything, it was George Miller that unified the California Presidents because of a general dislike of how he did certain things. <P>As President, I see myself as the person that deals with politics so that my club doesn't have to. I doubt if my club cares if there is a Board of Directors, much less what they do. Most but not all of my members just want to know where the bar is at the Regionals. A reputation that apparently is known across the country. If we are the Animal House of Fiero clubs than so be it, we are having a good time, even if we are on some Double Secret Probation with someone else.<P>Getting back to what Archie was saying, I will agree with him without hesitation that NIFE is without a doubt the best run Fiero club I have ever seen. I believe that they have just as much politics as anyone but it is overcome by the dedication of its membership as a whole. It does seem to be a different mindset here on the left coast than out there where you actually have things called Seasons. We Californians seriously freak out if it rains for longer than 4 hours. There are those that I am convinced believe that the Gods are angry at them and they atone for their sins by ramming the nearest car they can get to.<P>But as for CA style politics, I am at a loss to see what the problem is. I just don't believe that you are basing your observations on the comments held on the Fiero Forum. I know Im missing something when you go from "different groups" to Eric and Terry. <P>If you are refering to a difference of behavior among the groups I would agree. Golden Gate Fieros most likely has different agendas during their meetings than Fieros West. I know the last time I said, "This meeting has come to order," was in a swimming pool just before midnight in Palm Springs. But I flat out disagree that there are NO internal politics in any club in any degree. I believe that you need a little conflict to keep the club's vitality growing. <P>I for one am glad that FOCOA is staying out of this flame war. It would have gotten ugly in terms that have yet to be defined. I have spoken to Phil about it and he seems to have an attitude that I can agree with. I do not speak for him, I just report my interpretations of what he says. <P>Don't talk about the great club you want to be. <P>Just BE the club that you want to talk about.<P>   We shall see who is still standing in 5 years. FOA, and some others didn't do it. Its not to say that you won't because I doubt they could have generated this much exposure to themselves than with this flame war (by any other name is still a flame) you seem to have inadvertantly started.<BR>    With every every use of the acronym FOCOA, you are in the defensive position. Be like George, be offensive! Go do what you want to do. George put on a whole Regional by himself. Why? Because hes a stress mongering nutcase for one thing (I was a stress mongering nutcase too in San Diego), but also he had the bull headed determination to make it happen. <P>Go be an International club. <P>Some of us are getting bored with the rhetoric.||||reg||1
Z||000094||Cheever3000||12-19-2001||10:46 AM||||Please hear me out.  This may sound harsh at first, but please read to the end.<P>I am paying close attention to everyone's opinions, and I value those opinions greatly.  I knew when I started this that I would hear it from all sides, and that was my desire.  I intend to learn what the Fiero owners want, and do the best I can to help provide it.<P>It's true I broke my own promise about no negative public statements regarding FOCOA. So sue me - they break many promises, but I break one, that of bringing facts out in the open.  In our early days of forming this new club, it was widely agreed we shouldn't do that (bashing FOCOA).  I did not necessarily represent the others when I sent out the first post of this thread (btw, it also went to all club emails, the Fiero-List and several of the largest Yahoo clubs & groups).  I did inform them (the other officers in my club) before doing it - I got several saying do it, one who didn't know enough about FOCOA to say, and none suggesting I don't send it.  But... (why is mine always the biggest 'but' in the Fiero world)... the comparison of us to FOCOA was not something I or we started, it was a constant thing from the people and clubs we talked to.  It was always "What do you provide that they don't", and I got tired of it because of how little they actually provide, especially in light of their own words in their own websites.  <P>I don't regret saying it.  I still believe it had to be said.  When I first considered starting something new, I surveyed a handful of PFF members, most of whom I didn't even know.  Here's the response I got...<BR>"Yes, I am dissatisfied with FOCOA and, YES, I think it's time they either reorganize or WE start a new National Club!"<BR>"Got suckered into memberships and have ZILCH to show for it."<BR>"I am fully in agreement that FOCOA is doing a lousy job of it."<BR>"I'm not a member of FOCOA and probably never will be."<BR>"Poor organization, poor communication."<BR>"I'm not a member of FOCOA, and I have no desire to become one."<BR>"FOCOA sucks, rips people off and is actually doing the Fiero community a disservice."<BR>The only one who did not share such strong opinions said they have no need for ANY Fiero club, national OR local.  <P>So, I felt like somebody had to do something, and that survey turned into a movement.<P><B>Now, what I've learned from the response over "Let's talk about FOCOA" is...</B> there are at least three distinct groups of Fiero owners: those who don't like FOCOA, those who are diehard supporters of them, and those who prefer to stay out of this discussion entirely (a 4th group is those without the Internet).  I first thought of those who don't want to even hear the arguments & bickering as "pacifists", but it turns out there are very large numbers of them!  This was surprising to me, although you're probably saying "well DUH".  Since I want to make Fiero owners happy, I must listen to that group, and not dimiss them.  <P>So, the good thing about the entire discussion is that we're seeing what's really going on here.  We're finding out who we are and where we stand.  The question now is, what's in the best interests of all Fiero owners?  FOCOA is not going away, and I never said it should.  This new international club, as it is in these early days, is promising to some but dubious to others.  And then there are the numbers of people who don't see a need for a large organization.  We can't be all things to all people.  Maybe just the realization of how things are is enough.  But let's come together as much as possible, for the future of our Fiero nation.  I welcome all suggestions, both private and public, and I will listen and do my best to meet your wishes.  <P>One more thing.  I don't know where all this stuff about Terry comes from.  Prior PFF posts, unhappy Fiero Shop customers, I don't know.  But he can't do much in CFOG-I without my approval.  I can't do much without his approval.  And there are 18 other officers and directors who must approve as well, hopefully even more soon.  That's one of the main values of this club, to move as directed by all, not to be dictated by one person.  I'm aware that those quotes above about FOCOA could very well be about CFOG-I someday if we don't do the right thing.  Also please remember those of us in Officer and Director positions expect to eventually turn over those titles to others - I hope you'll be one of them.<P>I feel like starting a "Let's talk about CFOG-I" thread, but it's not my place.  Maybe it should be "Let's talk about ALL of us", but that's what this Forum already is.  Thanks again, Cliff!<BR> <P><BR> <P><BR>[This message has been edited by Cheever3000 (edited 12-19-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by Cheever3000 (edited 12-19-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000095||72vinman||12-20-2001||07:35 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cheever3000:<BR><B>And there are 18 other officers and directors who must approve as well, hopefully even more soon.  That's one of the main values of this club, to move as directed by all, not to be dictated by one person.  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>This I believe is the primary foundation that this club is being built on. The input of the membership is what steers the directors as to the type of club they want this to be. <BR>I believe all of the input thus far has provided many great ideas and many watch outs that we must keep in mind as we progress. Thanks to all of you for taking the time to respond.<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigvin2_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
